From f9a93c7bf85b621df49e157b90b894c0637ddf55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:38:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(build): pin the text files that tests read to LF

Tests search these tracked files for text that holds a line break. On a
Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true the files had CRLF, and the
searches failed. Pin AGENTS.md, site/**/*.md and the Heidenhain
contour.cnc stream to LF, like the golden files (#2840).

Fixes #3553

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .gitattributes | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitattributes b/.gitattributes
index 1f2d7997b..583ffaf17 100644
--- a/.gitattributes
+++ b/.gitattributes
@@ -32,6 +32,15 @@ examples/**/*.nc text eol=lf
 # The catalog refusal goldens are compared byte for byte by example_catalog.
 examples/catalog/**/refusal.txt text eol=lf
 
+# Tracked text that tests read and search for multi-line text (#3553): a CR
+# before the LF breaks the search. Pin each tree to LF in every checkout.
+# xtask light_tests and heavy_plan_tests read AGENTS.md.
+AGENTS.md text eol=lf
+# xtask catalog_links_tests and catalog_tests read the site guide pages.
+site/**/*.md text eol=lf
+# script_heidenhain_klartext edits this stream by text (a "...Z 15000\n" match).
+crates/post/tests/klartext/contour.cnc text eol=lf
+
 # Shell scripts run on macOS / Linux: a CR would break the shebang.
 *.sh text eol=lf
 
